# Without this file, Dockerfile's `COPY . .` bakes the real .env — API keys
# included — and the whole .venv into every image layer. Both are permanent:
# deleting them in a later layer does not remove them from the image history.

# --- Secrets ---
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem

# --- Virtualenvs and caches ---
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- VCS and editor ---
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/

# --- Local run artifacts (regenerated at runtime, often large) ---
logs/
reports/
reviews/
data/
*.log

# --- Local-only working docs ---
CLAUDE.md
plan.md
ARCHITECTURE.md
*walkthrough.md
*implementation_plan.md
resume*.md

# --- Tests (not needed in a runtime image) ---
tests/
test_*.py
